e1000: use phylink for a CE4100 described by the device tree

The CE4100 GbE MAC talks RGMII either to a PHY or straight to a switch
port. e1000 can only drive a PHY itself: with a switch there is nothing
on the MDIO bus, the PHY scan fails and probe returns -EIO.

If the device's OF node has a fixed-link or a phy-handle, create a
phylink instance from the node and let it own the link. The MAC is
forced to the speed, duplex and pause phylink resolves, and transmit is
enabled on link up. Link state, ethtool link and pause settings,
autonegotiation restart and the MII ioctls go to phylink, and e1000's
own PHY accesses are refused. Only rgmii phy modes are accepted, since
the MAC adds no delays.

Without either property, nothing changes.

Author: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
